# What `npm run format` must not touch.
#
# Prettier has no `.gitignore` awareness beyond `node_modules`, so anything
# generated or hand-authored has to be named here or the format script rewrites
# it. Everything below is excluded for a reason, not for tidiness.

# Build output and caches. Machine-written, never read by a human.
.next/
out/
coverage/
node_modules/

# THE PROJECT'S OWN BINDING DOCUMENTS.
#
# `CLAUDE.md`, `GIT.md`, `PROGRESS.md`, the architecture specification and the
# Next.js guidelines are hand-formatted prose whose line breaks carry meaning —
# tables, wrapped paragraphs, deliberate emphasis. Prettier reflows Markdown by
# its own rules and would rewrite all of it, producing an enormous diff over
# documents that are a source of truth. They are edited by hand and reviewed by
# eye; that is the standard they are held to.
.claude/

# Resolved by npm, not by anyone. Reformatting it guarantees a conflict on the
# next install and gains nothing.
package-lock.json

# The editor's own file, in the editor's own conventions (4-space here). It is
# not application source and does not follow the source's style.
.vscode/
